units-session.skool:32	title entry=gD010	Enemy hit-type code
units-session.skool:34	block entry=gD010	Which path removes a struck enemy.
units-session.skool:36	data-row entry=gD010	Enemy hit-type code read by #R$A010 to pick the removal path. 0 = a shot hit, set by the shot collision test #R$A020. A heavy shot such as the LASER bolt force-clears at #R$A030, and a plain shot checks armor at #R$A040. 1 = an ordinary enemy step, the default #R$A050 sets. It checks armor at #R$A040 and spares the armored robot. 2 = the bomb step, set by #R$A050 for the bomb only. That step takes the force-clear #R$A030, which empties any enemy slot, the armored robot too. The only routines that write it are #R$A020 and #R$A050 (#R$A050 setting 1 or 2).
units-session.skool:48	title entry=gD011	Heading code for the player
units-session.skool:50	data-row entry=gD011	Heading code for the player. Each active sprite's code comes from the #R$A060 table, written by #R$A070.
units-session.skool:53	title entry=gD012	Enemy hit type
units-session.skool:55	block entry=gD012	Which path removes a struck enemy.
units-session.skool:57	data-row entry=gD012	0 a shot, 1 an enemy, 2 the bomb
units-session.skool:59	title entry=gD013	Heading code
units-session.skool:61	data-row entry=gD013	Heading code of the player
